## scenario (hand-written, D5; not official data): data/synth/p13_it_service_desk/local_scenario.jsonl
{"name": "local_it_service_desk", "description": "Helpdesk Hub is the internal IT service desk of a mid-sized company, used by employees and by the IT support team. Employees submit support tickets for hardware failures, software installation, access requests and network problems, choosing a category and a priority and describing the issue. Support agents triage incoming tickets, assign them to themselves or to a specialist group, add internal notes and public comments, move tickets through the statuses open, in progress, waiting for user, resolved and closed, and escalate tickets that miss their service-level target. The desk keeps an asset inventory that links laptops, monitors, phones and software licenses to employees, so agents can see which devices a requester owns and record repairs or replacements. Employees can browse a knowledge base of troubleshooting articles, mark whether an article helped, and follow the history of their own tickets. Team leads review open workload per agent, overdue tickets and the satisfaction ratings that employees give after a ticket is resolved."}

## configuration (process environment only)
PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=$PWD/.cache/pycache
OPENAI_API_KEY="$DEEPSEEK_API_KEY"          # upstream key of the proxy (settings.synth.upstream_api_key_env)
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com      # upstream base URL of the proxy
AWM_SYN_OVERRIDE_MODEL=deepseek-flash

## command (attempt 1 and the resume are the same command)
$ uv run workbench synth run --scenarios 1 --out data/synth/p13_it_service_desk \
    --scenario-file data/synth/p13_it_service_desk/local_scenario.jsonl --execute

